  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICRC Appeals 2026-2029: Operations</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ICRC Appeals 2026-2029: Operations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This appraisal concerns a Decision on Contribution (Rule for Managing Contributions 5.4 &#xa7;) between Sida and the ICRC, to enter into a new four year agreement (2026-2029) and enable a humanitarian response in 20 crises for 2026. This decision concerns a financial contribution to the ICRC amounting to 495 MSEK in 2026, to support the ICRC Appeals.

The ICRC was selected as a central operational partner for the implementation of the 2025-2026 humanitarian strategy, based on its specific expertise in protection, IHL, and needs-based principled assistance, including in hard-to-reach areas, and capacity to intervene at scale.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det &#xe4;r ett beslut om insats mellan Sida och ICRC, genom ett nytt fyra&#xe5;rigt avtal (2026&#x2013;2029) som m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;r ett humanit&#xe4;rt st&#xf6;d i 20 kriser under 2026. Beslutet avser ett finansiellt bidrag till ICRC om 495 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r 2026, till st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r ICRC:s landappeller.

ICRC har valts ut som en central operativ partner f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;randet av den humanit&#xe4;ra strategin 2025&#x2013;2026, baserat p&#xe5; organisationens s&#xe4;rskilda expertis inom skydd, IHL och behovsbaserat, principstyrt bist&#xe5;nd, inklusive i sv&#xe5;rtillg&#xe4;ngliga omr&#xe5;den, samt dess kapacitet att agera i stor skala.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a Decision on Contribution between Sida and the ICRC, as part of a new four year agreement (2026-2029) to enable a humanitarian response in 20 crises for 2026. This decision concerns a financial contribution to the ICRC amounting to 495 MSEK in 2026, to support the ICRC Appeals.

The ICRC was selected as a central operational partner for the implementation of the 2025-2026 humanitarian strategy, based on its specific expertise in protection, IHL, and needs-based principled assistance, including in hard-to-reach areas, and capacity to intervene at scale.</narrative>
  </description>
